  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mulitple DGGF countries - Importing spices The Good Spice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF loan The Good Spice B.V. will be able to pre-finance to expend the import of spices from different origins. The Good Spice is the first company in the Dutch market to offer specialty spices in direct partnership with farmers. They source high-quality spices from all around the world that are produced without chemical pesticides or fertilizers and in the majority of our supply chains with regenerative methods. They will set up our own short and transparent supply chains and pay the farmer partners a fair price, based on the continuation and growth of their farms. The spices will be sold through the webshop (B2C), in specialized retail and to other sustainable food producers. They intent to educate and inspire customers and reconnect them with the origin of spices.The current origins are Sri Lanka, Hungary, South and North-East India for six different spices. In the coming two years they want to purchase new harvests from these origins and expand to ten origins and fifteen spices. This will lead to the indirect support of 65 jobs of which an estimated majority will be woman and the import of fair, premium and sustainable produced spices through transparent supply chains.</narrative>
  </description>
